WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.466
Whoa, a huge Pokémon battle!

2
00:00:04.533 --> 00:00:07.133
And it's taking place right here in town!

3
00:00:07.199 --> 00:00:10.100
- Wow!
- We should definitely go!

4
00:00:10.166 --> 00:00:12.799
- Pikachu!
- Wait. Is that...

5
00:00:14.399 --> 00:00:17.700
It is! Diantha's doing an exhibition battle!

6
00:00:17.766 --> 00:00:19.566
- Wonderful!
- Yeah.

7
00:00:19.633 --> 00:00:23.300
Awesome, all right! So who's Diantha, anyway?

8
00:00:24.599 --> 00:00:26.966
How can you not know who she is?

9
00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:30.400
She's the strongest Trainer in all of Kalos, that's who!

10
00:00:30.466 --> 00:00:33.100
- Yup. She's the Champion!
- Na-na-na!

11
00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:35.966
- Really? No kidding? Oh!
- Pika.

12
00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:39.699
Diantha the Champion, huh? I'm psyched!

13
00:00:39.766 --> 00:00:45.433
Not only is Diantha the Champion, she also happens to be a world-famous movie star!

14
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.400
- Movie star?
- Just have a look up there!

15
00:00:48.466 --> 00:00:50.133
Huh?

16
00:00:50.199 --> 00:00:53.866
That's her in the blockbuster My Sweet, Sweet Lady.

17
00:00:53.933 --> 00:00:55.933
Elegant, with a dignified presence!

18
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.666
The all-around perfect leading lady. I so admire her!

19
00:00:59.733 --> 00:01:01.666
- I do, too!
- Yes!

20
00:01:01.733 --> 00:01:05.766
- That's it! I'll challenge her!
- Pika!

21
00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:07.100
Huh?

22
00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:10.666
In that case, I'll ask her to take care of Clemont for me!

23
00:01:10.733 --> 00:01:14.433
- Na-na!
- Oh, that's even more ridiculous.

24
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.700
- Come on! Let's go see her!
- Pikachu!

25
00:01:16.766 --> 00:01:18.866
- Hey!
- Coming!

26
00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:20.933
Wait for me!

27
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.800
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

28
00:01:23.866 --> 00:01:27.366
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

29
00:01:27.433 --> 00:01:30.100
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

30
00:01:30.166 --> 00:01:33.200
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

31
00:01:33.266 --> 00:01:36.266
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

32
00:01:36.333 --> 00:01:39.500
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

33
00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:42.899
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

34
00:01:42.966 --> 00:01:45.333
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

35
00:01:45.399 --> 00:01:47.833
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

36
00:01:47.899 --> 00:01:50.899
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

37
00:02:00.066 --> 00:02:03.199
As our heroes continue their journey to Shalour City

38
00:02:03.266 --> 00:02:05.433
and Ash's next Gym battle challenge,

39
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.466
they decided to go and meet Diantha, the Champion!

40
00:02:09.533 --> 00:02:11.700
Excuse me, I'd like to get a word with Diantha.

41
00:02:11.766 --> 00:02:14.066
Everyone, settle down!

42
00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:15.466
Check out that crowd!

43
00:02:15.533 --> 00:02:21.066
Now, Diantha won't be seeing anyone or giving any interviews today!

44
00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:23.400
- You know what?
- We're out of luck.

45
00:02:23.466 --> 00:02:24.866
Shall we go back?

46
00:02:24.933 --> 00:02:28.433
- Hey, over here!
- Huh?

47
00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.666
Nice to see you!

48
00:02:29.733 --> 00:02:32.566
- Huh?
- Professor Sycamore!

49
00:02:33.566 --> 00:02:35.666
What are you doing here, Professor?

50
00:02:35.733 --> 00:02:39.500
There's only one reason for me to be away from my lab and what's that?

51
00:02:39.566 --> 00:02:43.233
You're here to do research on Mega Evolution, right?

52
00:02:43.299 --> 00:02:46.500
Still as perceptive as ever, Clemont. Exactly.

53
00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:51.500
I'm doing extensive research on Diantha's Gardevoir and its Mega Evolution.

54
00:02:51.566 --> 00:02:52.833
Oh.

55
00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.733
- Whoa, Gardevoir?
- It can really Mega Evolve?

56
00:02:55.799 --> 00:02:58.466
- It sure can!
- Wow. I want to see!

57
00:02:58.533 --> 00:03:01.533
Have you already seen Diantha, Professor?

58
00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.033
- I have.
- Huh?

59
00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.400
She's getting her makeup done in the next room.

60
00:03:05.466 --> 00:03:09.266
-Diantha's on the other side of that door!

61
00:03:09.333 --> 00:03:13.633
- Wow, wow, wow!
- We are so unbelievably lucky!

62
00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:16.966
Yes! I'm going to go challenge her to a battle!

63
00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:22.366
Sorry to keep you waiting, Professor. Oh, dear, I see you have guests, don't you?

64
00:03:22.433 --> 00:03:24.600
- Ah.
- It's Diantha for real!

65
00:03:24.666 --> 00:03:25.866
So pretty!

66
00:03:25.933 --> 00:03:27.600
Why, thank you.

67
00:03:27.666 --> 00:03:31.600
So did you reconsider what we spoke about earlier, Diantha?

68
00:03:31.666 --> 00:03:35.833
You must mean about me lending you this Key Stone, right?

69
00:03:35.899 --> 00:03:38.333
Key Stone?

70
00:03:38.399 --> 00:03:40.866
I'm sorry, but I'm afraid I can't.

71
00:03:40.933 --> 00:03:44.666
If there's anything else I can help you with, I'd be happy to,

72
00:03:44.733 --> 00:03:48.399
but this Key Stone is part of the bond I have with Gardevoir.

73
00:03:49.633 --> 00:03:53.066
- Bond?
- I can't lend it to anyone. Sorry.

74
00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:57.799
- I understand how you feel, but please.
- All right, then.

75
00:03:57.866 --> 00:04:02.299
Well, how about the next time I visit Lumiose City, if I have some time.

76
00:04:02.366 --> 00:04:06.600
Not going to happen! No way! Diantha's schedule is already jam-packed!

77
00:04:06.666 --> 00:04:10.033
Right now we haven't any plans to visit Lumiose City!

78
00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:13.766
Your expression is as cute as ever when you get angry, you know?

79
00:04:13.833 --> 00:04:18.233
Why don't we discuss this whole scheduling conflict

80
00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.700
in a civilized way over a little dinner?

81
00:04:20.766 --> 00:04:22.733
No thanks!

82
00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.933
- You're on soon. Are you all set to go?
- Yes.

83
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.800
You're all welcome to stay for the exhibition battle.

84
00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.733
-Pika!

85
00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:36.733
And now for today's main event!

86
00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:38.733
Please welcome our Trainers!

87
00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:44.233
Crowned Best of Brackish Town just last year, say hi to Magnus!

88
00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:50.033
He'll be facing off against the elegant Kalos region Champion, Diantha!

89
00:04:50.099 --> 00:04:53.466
-Yay, Diantha!

90
00:04:55.066 --> 00:04:58.966
Professor, what's with that Key Stone you two were talking about before?

91
00:04:59.033 --> 00:05:03.766
You see, the Key Stone is crucial for a Pokémon to Mega Evolve.

92
00:05:03.833 --> 00:05:06.833
The stone a Trainer possesses is called a Key Stone

93
00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:10.333
and the stone a Pokémon possesses is called a Mega Stone.

94
00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:14.400
- Key Stone and Mega Stone...
- All right, Gardevoir, it's time.

95
00:05:14.466 --> 00:05:17.300
Let's show the fans a spectacular battle!

96
00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.000
Gardevoir.

97
00:05:20.066 --> 00:05:23.000
- The Champion's Pokémon!
- Pika.

98
00:05:24.099 --> 00:05:26.800
Gardevoir, the Embrace Pokémon.

99
00:05:26.866 --> 00:05:30.033
Gardevoir will use all of its psychic energy to protect a Trainer

100
00:05:30.099 --> 00:05:33.599
it has made a deep connection with.

101
00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:36.666
Hey, look! Gardevoir's wearing a pendant as well!

102
00:05:36.733 --> 00:05:40.066
- Yeah, you're right!
- That's Gardevoir's Mega Stone.

103
00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:42.066
Mega Stones have many different names,

104
00:05:42.133 --> 00:05:44.500
depending on the Pokémon that Mega Evolves.

105
00:05:44.566 --> 00:05:48.133
In Gardervoir's case, its Mega Stone is called Gardevoirite.

106
00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.866
I see! As long as you have both a Key Stone

107
00:05:52.933 --> 00:05:55.599
and a Mega Stone, a Pokémon can Mega Evolve!

108
00:05:55.666 --> 00:05:56.733
So cool!

109
00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:59.333
- That's actually not enough.
- Huh?

110
00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.166
A Pokémon can't Mega Evolve

111
00:06:01.233 --> 00:06:04.366
unless the hearts of Trainer and Pokémon become one.

112
00:06:04.433 --> 00:06:05.733
Hearts become one?

113
00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:09.966
It means they need to have an exceptionally strong bond between them.

114
00:06:10.033 --> 00:06:12.233
Of course! That's what Diantha meant

115
00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:15.900
when she said the Key Stone is part of their bond.

116
00:06:15.966 --> 00:06:19.099
Ooh, it sounds like the Champion's Gardevoir

117
00:06:19.166 --> 00:06:21.333
possesses the power to Mega Evolve.

118
00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:24.133
Yeah! That's what I'm talking about!

119
00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.900
Diantha's a great actress, just like myself.

120
00:06:26.966 --> 00:06:29.133
Oh. How did I forget that?

121
00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:33.633
A fellow great actress's Pokémon is worthy to be my Pokémon

122
00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:36.966
and Gardevoir will be my Pokémon, mark my word!

123
00:06:37.033 --> 00:06:41.299
Marked! In addition, the Boss will love a Pokémon that can Mega Evolve.

124
00:06:41.366 --> 00:06:43.833
Now! Absol, let's go!

125
00:06:45.166 --> 00:06:46.566
Sol!

126
00:06:46.633 --> 00:06:48.566
Gardevoir and Absol.

127
00:06:48.633 --> 00:06:50.666
Absol, the Disaster Pokémon.

128
00:06:50.733 --> 00:06:52.866
When disasters are detected with its horn,

129
00:06:52.933 --> 00:06:56.033
Absol comes down from the mountains to warn people.

130
00:06:56.099 --> 00:06:57.666
Here we go.

131
00:06:57.733 --> 00:06:59.766
Now, let the battle begin!

132
00:07:03.566 --> 00:07:06.099
- You may go first, Magnus!
- Thank you!

133
00:07:06.166 --> 00:07:08.033
Absol, use Bite!

134
00:07:08.099 --> 00:07:10.233
Sol!

135
00:07:10.299 --> 00:07:12.099
Hm.

136
00:07:12.166 --> 00:07:14.400
-It's gone!

137
00:07:14.466 --> 00:07:18.599
Absol! Behind you! Now use Quick Attack!

138
00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:29.066
It appears Diantha and Gardevoir can communicate by making eye contact!

139
00:07:29.133 --> 00:07:31.900
- Huh? Oh, wow, they can do that?
- Pika. Pika.

140
00:07:31.966 --> 00:07:34.000
I'd have to say it's their strong bond

141
00:07:34.066 --> 00:07:36.566
that allows them to successfully accomplish that.

142
00:07:36.633 --> 00:07:38.400
All right, use Psycho Cut!

143
00:07:38.466 --> 00:07:42.400
Absol!

144
00:07:42.466 --> 00:07:45.933
- Hm. Use Shadow Ball!
- Gardevoir!

145
00:07:52.233 --> 00:07:58.266
-Uh... In that case, use Perish Song!

146
00:07:58.333 --> 00:08:01.333
And checkmate! Use Moonblast!

147
00:08:14.066 --> 00:08:17.533
Absol is unable to battle! Gardevoir is the winner,

148
00:08:17.599 --> 00:08:20.033
which means, the victory goes to Diantha!

149
00:08:20.099 --> 00:08:22.333
- Incredible!
- Diantha's amazing!

150
00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.033
- Wonderful!
- She's strong.

151
00:08:24.099 --> 00:08:25.900
Gardevoir didn't Mega Evolve.

152
00:08:25.966 --> 00:08:28.033
- And they still won!
- Awesome!

153
00:08:30.366 --> 00:08:33.033
Yeah! I'm going to get her to battle me!

154
00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:36.666
I'll ask her again too for my research.

155
00:08:39.633 --> 00:08:41.699
- Whoa! They're all here again!
- Please calm down!

156
00:08:41.766 --> 00:08:45.466
Diantha's shooting a movie right now, so she's already left the stadium!

157
00:08:45.533 --> 00:08:46.699
-What?

158
00:08:46.766 --> 00:08:49.300
- Man!
- She's already gone?

159
00:08:49.366 --> 00:08:52.266
- Movie stars sure are busy.
- That's too bad.

160
00:08:52.333 --> 00:08:55.100
- So, what do we do now?
- Wait.

161
00:08:55.166 --> 00:08:57.733
Just a sec. Let's go here!

162
00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:01.966
It says they make the best chocolate cake anywhere! Let's find out!

163
00:09:02.033 --> 00:09:04.033
- I want to go, too!
- Sounds great!

164
00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:06.766
- Would you like to come, Professor?
- Sure do!

165
00:09:06.833 --> 00:09:09.600
First, I have to send the footage to the research lab.

166
00:09:09.666 --> 00:09:11.533
- I'll meet you there.
- Great!

167
00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:15.800
Huh. Oh, there's a crowd here, too!

168
00:09:15.866 --> 00:09:19.400
It seems like there's a huge crowd everywhere we go today.

169
00:09:19.466 --> 00:09:21.866
- Yeah.
- They're not getting me down!

170
00:09:21.933 --> 00:09:23.033
Let's move it!

171
00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:25.266
- Right with you!
- Huh?

172
00:09:25.333 --> 00:09:27.166
I'm exhausted!

173
00:09:27.233 --> 00:09:30.133
But we finally managed to get a piece of cake.

174
00:09:30.199 --> 00:09:33.566
Can't wait to try some! Now, let's see...

175
00:09:33.633 --> 00:09:36.100
- Wait!
- Huh?

176
00:09:36.166 --> 00:09:39.433
What are you thinking? That slice is for the four of us!

177
00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.300
Ah! This one slice?

178
00:09:41.366 --> 00:09:45.766
That's right! If we're not splitting it, I'll just eat it all by myself!

179
00:09:45.833 --> 00:09:48.566
- Hey! I want some!
- Na-na!

180
00:09:48.633 --> 00:09:50.800
One slice, that's all?

181
00:09:50.866 --> 00:09:53.300
Sounds like that's my cue!

182
00:09:53.366 --> 00:09:57.800
The future is now, thanks to science!

183
00:09:57.866 --> 00:09:59.533
Clemontic Gear on!

184
00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:03.600
I thought that we would encounter a situation precisely like this one!

185
00:10:03.666 --> 00:10:08.066
- I call it the Precisely Even Cut-o-matic!
- Precisely Even Cut-o-matic?

186
00:10:08.133 --> 00:10:12.466
Like the name suggests, it eliminates the imperfection from eyeballing a cut,

187
00:10:12.533 --> 00:10:15.833
making equal slices with 0.1 millimeter precision!

188
00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:18.699
We've got this one piece! It's got to be right!

189
00:10:18.766 --> 00:10:21.233
All right, here we go!

190
00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:24.966
- You're sold out already?
- I'm so very sorry.

191
00:10:25.033 --> 00:10:30.033
Oh! What a tragedy! To think I came all this way just to have a piece

192
00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.833
of this shop's award-winning chocolate cake.

193
00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:35.199
Oh. The end of the world.

194
00:10:35.266 --> 00:10:38.633
- End of the world?
- That's disappointment!

195
00:10:38.699 --> 00:10:43.166
Ma'am, if you're okay with a bite, we'll be happy to share ours with you!

196
00:10:43.233 --> 00:10:45.699
- You will?
- Sure!

197
00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.166
Haven't I seen you all before?

198
00:10:49.233 --> 00:10:53.100
- Huh?
- Hi. It's me.

199
00:10:53.166 --> 00:10:56.833
- Huh, Diantha?
- Pika!

200
00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:59.866
Shh.

201
00:10:59.933 --> 00:11:02.766
Who's that Pokémon?

202
00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:09.300
It's Gardevoir!

203
00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:15.000
Now, where were we?

204
00:11:17.833 --> 00:11:20.133
- All right!
- Science is so amazing!

205
00:11:20.199 --> 00:11:23.300
- Pika! Pika!
- Help yourself, Diantha!

206
00:11:23.366 --> 00:11:26.133
- Thank you!
- Let's eat!

207
00:11:26.199 --> 00:11:29.333
Mm!

208
00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:30.466
Mm!

209
00:11:30.533 --> 00:11:32.466
So good!

210
00:11:32.533 --> 00:11:35.133
Wow, best chocolate cake I ever had!

211
00:11:35.199 --> 00:11:40.066
It is! The sweetness brings the bold bitterness and acidity together perfectly.

212
00:11:40.133 --> 00:11:42.199
A memorable cake, for sure!

213
00:11:42.266 --> 00:11:44.333
You certainly know your cake!

214
00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:45.900
I just adore desserts.

215
00:11:45.966 --> 00:11:47.699
Mm. I do, too!

216
00:11:47.766 --> 00:11:50.066
- Me, too!
- Na-na!

217
00:11:50.133 --> 00:11:52.133
Whenever I visit a town for work,

218
00:11:52.199 --> 00:11:55.466
I always look forward to sampling their most popular desserts,

219
00:11:55.533 --> 00:11:57.033
whether I'm busy or not.

220
00:11:57.100 --> 00:12:02.100
Movie star and Champion, Juggling two jobs must be challenging, to say the least.

221
00:12:02.166 --> 00:12:06.600
But I do it out of love, so it's really not work at all.

222
00:12:06.666 --> 00:12:10.900
- You're so amazing!
- That's right! You're a keeper! Ha-ha!

223
00:12:10.966 --> 00:12:14.100
Won't you please take care of my brother?

224
00:12:14.166 --> 00:12:17.133
- Take care?
- I told you to stop this!

225
00:12:17.199 --> 00:12:19.666
You see, my brother is a bit shy,

226
00:12:19.733 --> 00:12:24.199
so I thought it would be good if he married a dependable woman like you.

227
00:12:24.266 --> 00:12:26.199
Me marry your brother?

228
00:12:26.266 --> 00:12:28.433
It was just a joke!

229
00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:30.000
I wasn't joking!

230
00:12:30.066 --> 00:12:33.866
Excuse me. Diantha? Please have a Pokémon battle with me!

231
00:12:33.933 --> 00:12:35.266
Huh? You?

232
00:12:35.333 --> 00:12:36.733
- Ash!
- Huh?

233
00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:39.599
You must know Diantha doesn't get much private time

234
00:12:39.666 --> 00:12:42.199
and here you are bothering her this way!

235
00:12:42.266 --> 00:12:46.666
Yeah, but I want to be a Pokémon Master so having a battle with you

236
00:12:46.733 --> 00:12:50.833
would be awesome because you're the Champion! Please!

237
00:12:55.733 --> 00:12:57.833
- All right.
- Huh?

238
00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:00.766
I usually turn down unofficial battle requests,

239
00:13:00.833 --> 00:13:03.933
but you shared your chocolate cake with me. Just this once.

240
00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:07.400
- All right! She said yes, Pikachu!
- Pikachu!

241
00:13:07.466 --> 00:13:09.800
A battle against the Champion, eh?

242
00:13:09.866 --> 00:13:11.800
Professor!

243
00:13:11.866 --> 00:13:15.533
If you don't mind, I'd like to come watch it.

244
00:13:19.133 --> 00:13:21.566
I see you're going to use Pikachu, right?

245
00:13:21.633 --> 00:13:23.566
- Right!
- Pikachu!

246
00:13:23.633 --> 00:13:27.066
Now, I really hope to see a Mega Evolution this time!

247
00:13:27.133 --> 00:13:29.266
Battle begin!

248
00:13:32.133 --> 00:13:35.466
- You may go first, Ash.
- Pikachu, use Iron Tail!

249
00:13:35.533 --> 00:13:39.866
Pika! Chu! Pika!

250
00:13:39.933 --> 00:13:43.599
- Now follow it with Quick Attack!
- Pika! Pi! Pi! Pi!

251
00:13:43.666 --> 00:13:46.400
-Ka! Ka! Pikachu!

252
00:13:46.466 --> 00:13:48.933
- Use Electro Ball!
- Pika!

253
00:13:50.633 --> 00:13:57.233
- Now Thunderbolt!
- Pikachu!

254
00:13:57.300 --> 00:14:00.533
- Huh? Wow, it dodged Thunderbolt too.
- Pika?

255
00:14:00.599 --> 00:14:03.733
- Pikachu's moves didn't do a thing!
- Wow!

256
00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:07.000
And checkmate. Shadow Ball, go!

257
00:14:07.066 --> 00:14:10.333
Gardevoir!

258
00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:12.833
Pika! Pika!

259
00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:15.666
Pikachu!

260
00:14:18.933 --> 00:14:21.800
- Ash!
- Oh, man. That hurt.

261
00:14:21.866 --> 00:14:24.633
But I'm fine. Hey, Buddy, are you okay, too?

262
00:14:24.699 --> 00:14:25.800
Pikachu!

263
00:14:25.866 --> 00:14:28.533
- All right, the real battle starts now!
- Pika!

264
00:14:28.599 --> 00:14:31.633
He really cares about his Pokémon.

265
00:14:31.699 --> 00:14:33.900
Ash is a very passionate Trainer!

266
00:14:37.966 --> 00:14:40.500
Prepare for trouble, actress to actress!

267
00:14:40.566 --> 00:14:42.900
But two are too many so more is really less!

268
00:14:42.966 --> 00:14:45.400
To protect the world from competition!

269
00:14:45.466 --> 00:14:48.066
In keeping with the actor's tradition!

270
00:14:48.133 --> 00:14:51.166
To perform with great style, truth and love!

271
00:14:51.233 --> 00:14:54.599
To allow great talent to fit like a glove!

272
00:14:54.666 --> 00:14:56.466
- Jessie!
- And James!

273
00:14:56.533 --> 00:14:59.766
Team Rocket blasts off with award-winning grace!

274
00:14:59.833 --> 00:15:02.900
Surrender now or prepare for us in your face!

275
00:15:02.966 --> 00:15:04.833
Meowth, on the case!

276
00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:09.099
Gardevoir... Gardevoir...

277
00:15:09.166 --> 00:15:11.333
Team Rocket! You're doing it again?

278
00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:15.433
They're a bunch of really bad guys who go around stealing other people's Pokémon!

279
00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:18.333
They steal Pokémon? What despicable people!

280
00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:22.066
Why, thank you. We'll wear that as a badge of honor.

281
00:15:22.133 --> 00:15:26.099
Since I'm the greatest actress of all time, I accept your kind words.

282
00:15:26.166 --> 00:15:32.000
- Quick, Gardevoir! Shadow Ball!
- Gardevoir! Huh?

283
00:15:32.066 --> 00:15:33.433
Oh, smashing!

284
00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:37.300
The only thing getting in and out of this box is sunlight, dig?

285
00:15:37.366 --> 00:15:39.333
And, curtain up!

286
00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:40.466
Huh?

287
00:15:41.766 --> 00:15:43.900
Bye-bye, chump guys!

288
00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:48.199
- They're gone!
- They flew away!

289
00:15:48.266 --> 00:15:50.800
Don't worry. I'll take us right to them.

290
00:15:50.866 --> 00:15:55.566
Diantha, wait. Do you know where Gardevoir is?

291
00:15:55.633 --> 00:15:57.166
Yes.

292
00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:03.433
-Come on, Clemont, hurry up!

293
00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:07.599
It happened when I was in the Lapidarian Highlands for a film shoot.

294
00:16:07.666 --> 00:16:10.699
Ah! That's one of the last unexplored regions in the world!

295
00:16:10.766 --> 00:16:16.066
Yes, that's right. A thick fog rolled into the area while we were shooting.

296
00:16:17.800 --> 00:16:19.500
Huh?

297
00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.866
It's Gardevoir!

298
00:16:35.933 --> 00:16:38.099
Gardevoir.

299
00:16:39.099 --> 00:16:41.066
Diantha!

300
00:16:41.133 --> 00:16:43.300
Gardevoir.

301
00:16:43.366 --> 00:16:46.900
Later, my manager Kathi Lee told me that Gardevoir's had appeared

302
00:16:46.966 --> 00:16:49.000
from its Poké Ball on its own!

303
00:16:49.066 --> 00:16:52.733
It then guided everyone to exactly where I had gotten lost.

304
00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:57.000
Hm. Could the stones be responsible for what happened? I wonder.

305
00:16:57.066 --> 00:16:59.400
Maybe Diantha's and Gardevoir's hearts were connected

306
00:16:59.466 --> 00:17:01.166
and called out to each other!

307
00:17:01.233 --> 00:17:03.500
Did you say it was our hearts?

308
00:17:03.566 --> 00:17:06.000
- I think Ash is right!
- Yup!

309
00:17:06.066 --> 00:17:10.366
Hm. Huh? Gardevoir's up ahead!

310
00:17:10.433 --> 00:17:12.366
Huh?

311
00:17:13.366 --> 00:17:15.200
It's them!

312
00:17:16.266 --> 00:17:19.766
So let's review. This Gardevoir can Mega Evolve.

313
00:17:19.833 --> 00:17:23.933
And once it's safely into the Boss's hands, we'll evolve into big shots!

314
00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:26.166
A major mega-promotion!

315
00:17:29.566 --> 00:17:32.933
- There they are.
- Ash, I want you all to stay here.

316
00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:35.600
- Uh, but...
- It'll be fine.

317
00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:41.133
All right. You listen. I want my Gardevoir!

318
00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:43.366
- Huh?
- How'd she find us?

319
00:17:43.433 --> 00:17:45.500
Huh! The how means nothing!

320
00:17:45.566 --> 00:17:48.500
We'll just see. Now, Gardevoir!

321
00:17:48.566 --> 00:17:51.766
Let's show them a few things about a strong bond!

322
00:17:52.766 --> 00:17:54.000
Gar...

323
00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:03.566
Gardevoir!

324
00:18:08.133 --> 00:18:09.399
Look at that light.

325
00:18:09.466 --> 00:18:10.833
- Is it...?
- It is!

326
00:18:10.899 --> 00:18:13.033
That's when a Pokémon Mega Evolves!

327
00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:16.100
Gardevoir, now Mega Evolve!

328
00:18:16.166 --> 00:18:21.200
Gardevoir!

329
00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:32.533
Gardevoir!

330
00:18:32.600 --> 00:18:35.433
- Yeah, check it out!
- Wow! It Mega Evolved!

331
00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:37.466
- What a sight!
- Excellent!

332
00:18:37.533 --> 00:18:39.333
- It's so cool!
- Marvelous!

333
00:18:39.399 --> 00:18:41.399
Uh, I think we're in trouble.

334
00:18:41.466 --> 00:18:45.333
Chill! Our box can deal with anything that galoot dishes out!

335
00:18:45.399 --> 00:18:49.500
- Use Shadow Ball!
- Gardevoir!

336
00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:58.066
- Our box is junk!
- Such pompous power!

337
00:18:59.033 --> 00:19:02.966
And checkmate! Excellent work. Use Moonblast.

338
00:19:06.533 --> 00:19:09.600
- Let's beat a hasty retreat!
- Step on it!

339
00:19:09.666 --> 00:19:11.833
Gardevoir!

340
00:19:13.899 --> 00:19:17.933
We're blasting off again!

341
00:19:18.933 --> 00:19:21.366
- Awesome!
- You did it!

342
00:19:21.433 --> 00:19:23.433
Gardevoir.

343
00:19:25.266 --> 00:19:27.066
- Huh?
- Hey look, it changed back!

344
00:19:27.133 --> 00:19:31.000
Right. What makes Mega Evolution different from ordinary Evolution is

345
00:19:31.066 --> 00:19:34.466
it isn't permanent.

346
00:19:34.533 --> 00:19:38.466
-That's what I call perfect timing.

347
00:19:38.533 --> 00:19:42.200
Diantha!

348
00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:49.466
Ash, I realize we weren't able to finish our battle together, but it was fun.

349
00:19:49.533 --> 00:19:51.966
- I thought it was fun too!
- Pika!

350
00:19:52.033 --> 00:19:54.500
Thanks so much to all of you.

351
00:19:54.566 --> 00:19:56.200
Will we ever see you again?

352
00:19:56.266 --> 00:20:00.666
- I want to talk to you more.
- Now, you shouldn't bother her like that!

353
00:20:00.733 --> 00:20:03.033
I'm sorry. I have a movie shoot to get to.

354
00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:05.133
I want to thank you for showing me the bond

355
00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:08.100
that's so crucial for a Pokémon to Mega Evolve.

356
00:20:08.166 --> 00:20:11.700
I'm glad I was able to help. Take care!

357
00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:16.000
Diantha?

358
00:20:16.066 --> 00:20:19.533
Right now I'm training really hard to enter the Kalos League,

359
00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:22.666
so when I win, will you battle with me again?

360
00:20:22.733 --> 00:20:26.233
That's a tall order, but that's the spirit.

361
00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:28.899
Yes! I'll look forward to it!

362
00:20:31.233 --> 00:20:35.766
An encounter with Diantha has given our heroes and Professor Sycamore

363
00:20:35.833 --> 00:20:38.966
a deeper look into the mysteries of Mega Evolution!

364
00:20:39.033 --> 00:20:44.100
Now it's off once again to Shalour City, as the journey continues!
